# Copy to `.env` (never commit secrets)

# Amazon RDS PostgreSQL in us-east-2 (example)
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOSTNAME:5432/stage_director_pro?sslmode=require"

# REQUIRED — Auth.js throws MissingSecret if unset
AUTH_SECRET="use_a_long_random_string_at_least_32_chars"

# Optional; dev base URL used in SES intake emails (link to inbox)
APP_BASE_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Dev only — if you open the site via the LAN "Network" URL (e.g. http://172.20.x.x:3000), Next blocks API/Server Actions
# unless that host is listed. Comma-separated hostnames only (no scheme/port), matched to Origin.
# NEXT_ALLOWED_DEV_ORIGINS=172.20.128.1

# Amazon SES — new intake + Director production files uploads notify INTAKE_NOTIFY_EMAIL; director-invite & password-reset use SES_FROM_EMAIL (sandbox: verify each recipient address).
AWS_REGION=us-east-2
# SES_FROM_EMAIL=verified-sender@yourdomain.com
# INTAKE_NOTIFY_EMAIL=producer1@ulis.com,producer2@ulis.com
# Use IAM user keys or SSO profile AWS_REGION + default credential chain — do not paste keys here

# Private S3 bucket for producer-only contract & compliance uploads (SSE-S3 objects; app issues presigned GETs).
# Also stores v2 show media under `uls-stage-director/project-show-media/`, Director production files (portal reference AV) under `uls-stage-director/project-director-shares/`, and the reusable media library under `uls-stage-director/show-media-library/` (same bucket IAM: Put/Get/Delete).
# AWS_S3_ATTACHMENTS_BUCKET=uls-stage-director-attachments-dev
#
# **AWS_REGION** must match the bucket’s region (e.g. us-east-2). Wrong region → presigned URLs fail with SignatureDoesNotMatch / 403 on PUT and GET.
#
# Browser presigned PUTs: `@aws-sdk/client-s3` **3.729+** auto-adds CRC32 to PutObject signatures; URLs then contain `x-amz-sdk-checksum-algorithm=CRC32`, but the browser sends only Content-Type → **403 PUT**. Dependencies are pinned to **3.726.1** (last line before that default), plus `requestChecksumCalculation: WHEN_REQUIRED` / optional env `AWS_REQUEST_CHECKSUM_CALCULATION=WHEN_REQUIRED`.
# The S3 request presigner intentionally leaves **`Content-Type` unsigned** (`X-Amz-SignedHeaders` often `host` only). Clients must PUT **without** that header (upload forms use `new Blob([file], { type: "" })`); MIME is inferred on finalize from key filename + lane when HeadObject reports a generic type.
#
# IAM for the Vercel user (access keys or role) must allow the same operations on every prefix the app writes or reads — missing `project-show-media/*` breaks uploads (403 PUT) AND waveform/proxy playback (502 on `/api/show-media/[id]?proxy=1` with upstream `AccessDenied`):
# Grant s3:PutObject, s3:GetObject, s3:HeadObject, s3:DeleteObject, s3:CopyObject on Resources:
#   arn:aws:s3:::YOUR-BUCKET/uls-stage-director/project-attachments/*
#   arn:aws:s3:::YOUR-BUCKET/uls-stage-director/project-show-media/*
#   arn:aws:s3:::YOUR-BUCKET/uls-stage-director/project-director-shares/*
#   arn:aws:s3:::YOUR-BUCKET/uls-stage-director/show-media-library/*
# (CopyObject reads the source key and writes the destination key server-side.)
#
# Troubleshooting staging: PUT returns **403** in Network (response body `<Code>`) while presign `/api/producer/show-media/presign` returns 200 ⇒ not a CORS block; fix IAM bucket policy / KMS bucket rules or align signing region with the bucket.
#
# Browser uploads (show media / media library / Production files) use presigned PUT to this bucket — the bucket MUST have CORS
# configured or uploads fail in the browser with “blocked by CORS policy” / “No Access-Control-Allow-Origin”.
#
# In AWS Console: S3 → bucket → Permissions → Cross-origin resource sharing (CORS) → Edit, or use PutBucketCors / CLI with JSON like:
# [
#   {
#     "AllowedHeaders": ["*"],
#     "AllowedMethods": ["GET", "HEAD", "PUT"],
#     "AllowedOrigins": [
#       "http://localhost:3000",
#       "http://127.0.0.1:3000"
#     ],
#     "ExposeHeaders": ["ETag"],
#     "MaxAgeSeconds": 3000
#   },
#   {
#     "AllowedHeaders": ["*"],
#     "AllowedMethods": ["GET", "HEAD", "PUT"],
#     "AllowedOrigins": ["https://YOUR-PRODUCTION-HOST.example"],
#     "ExposeHeaders": ["ETag"],
#     "MaxAgeSeconds": 3000
#   },
#   {
#     "AllowedHeaders": ["*"],
#     "AllowedMethods": ["GET", "HEAD", "PUT"],
#     "AllowedOrigins": ["https://uls-stage-director-pro.vercel.app"],
#     "ExposeHeaders": ["ETag"],
#     "MaxAgeSeconds": 3000
#   }
# ]
# Replace production host when you ship. **Vercel Preview** deploys each get their own `https://*-*.vercel.app` hostname — either add those origins too or route staging through one stable Preview URL / custom domain and CORS-list only that origin.
# GET/HEAD support portal playback URLs; PUT is required for uploads. AllowedHeaders "*" must cover `x-amz-server-side-encryption` — presigned uploads use SSE-S3 (matches server PutObject); clients omit `Content-Type` on PUT but send that encryption header (.env stays aligned with ATTACHMENTS_PRESIGNED_PUT_HEADERS).

# Optional: GET /api/cron/retention-preview with Authorization: Bearer <secret> lists projects past the 36‑month retention anchor without legal hold (runbook aid; does not delete data).
# CRON_RETENTION_PREVIEW_SECRET=

# Optional; Auth.js issuer URL if needed behind custom host
# AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"

# Stripe — ULS Standard account (payments to ULS; Connect deferred per product spec).
# Plan: keep TEST keys (`sk_test_…`, matching webhook secrets, Dashboard test mode) through v1/v2; adopt `sk_live_…` after v3 ship — no app code forces live.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...
# Stripe Dashboard webhook URL ends with /api/webhooks/stripe (prefix with APP_BASE_URL). Enable invoice.* events.
# Dev: stripe listen --forward-to localhost:3000/api/webhooks/stripe

# DocuSign Connect (JSON SIM) — mirror envelope status metadata into Postgres.
# Connect is PER DocuSign account/environment: developer envelopes under apps-d must use Connect in DEMO Admin:
#   https://admindemo.docusign.com/authenticate?goTo=connect
# Production Connect at admin.docusign.com does NOT receive events from apps-d / demo envelopes.
# 1. In matching DocuSign Admin » Connect » Custom Connect » JSON SIM » URL = APP_BASE_URL + /api/webhooks/docusign
# 2. Enable “Include HMAC” / Basic HMAC and paste the SAME secret below.
DOCUSIGN_CONNECT_HMAC_SECRET=

# DocuSign REST (JWT) — optional; for server-to-server API calls (not required for Connect mirror only).
# Uses the same DEMO vs production host as DOCUSIGN_USE_DEMO (see docusign-admin.ts).
# Create an Integration Key + RSA keypair in Apps and Keys; impersonate sends as DOCUSIGN_USER_ID after one-time consent.
# DOCUSIGN_INTEGRATION_KEY=
# DOCUSIGN_USER_ID=uuid-of-impersonated-user
# DOCUSIGN_RSA_PRIVATE_KEY="-----BEGIN RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n...\n-----END RSA PRIVATE KEY-----\n"
# Optional override (otherwise account-d.docusign.com vs account.docusign.com):
# DOCUSIGN_AUTH_SERVER=account-d.docusign.com

# DEMO console links (recommended for dev): DOCUSIGN_USE_DEMO=true
# DOCUSIGN_USE_DEMO=true
